          "class": "RULED",
          "reason": "Actual gradient and true Gaussian-output pushforward. No posterior/RGO/HMC kernel equality or supplied law."
        },
        {
          "definition": "m_s=integral identity dK_s; all a:E,t:real exponentials",
          "class": "RULED / TYPING",
          "reason": "Actual own-mean centering; first Bochner/domain conclusions produced before numerical bound. Signed t/zero a retained."
        }
      ],
      "mathematical_findings": "The same p/G/K and all old genuine domain outputs are preserved. The new conjunction adds exact integral exp(t*inner(a,w-ownmean))<=exp(eta_s*t^2*norm(a)^2/2) under the same K_s. Choosing t=1,a=u recovers source4.3; conversely u=t*a gives every signed parameter. The directional scalar Lipschitz constant norm(a)*sqrt(eta_s) has square eta_s*norm(a)^2, with no kappa/dimension factor. Full eta>0 and fixed-eta comparison conditions remain exact. Gaussian output law is not posterior RGO or smoothed-gradient mean."
